---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import portrait from '../assets/portrait.jpg';
import { SITE, url } from '../lib/site';

const career = [
  { when: '2024 – now', what: 'Director of Gen AI', where: 'Euromonitor International, Singapore' },
  { when: '2024 – 2026', what: 'Country Manager, Singapore', where: 'Euromonitor’s hub for Southeast Asia' },
  { when: '2021 – 2024', what: 'Head of Transformation', where: 'Euromonitor International, Singapore' },
  { when: '2017 – 2021', what: 'Head of Research Technology, and Head of Food and Nutrition', where: 'Euromonitor International, London' },
  { when: '2013 – 2017', what: 'Packaged Food Industry Manager', where: 'Euromonitor International, London' },
  { when: '2009 – 2013', what: 'Industrial Analyst, then Senior Analyst, Retailing', where: 'Euromonitor International, Vilnius and London' },
  { when: '2005 – 2009', what: 'Analyst, economics lecturer and market-entry consultant', where: 'Beijing' },
  { when: '2002 – 2005', what: 'BSc Economics', where: 'SOAS, University of London' },
];
---

<Base title="About" description="Biography of Lamine Lahouasnia, Director of Gen AI at Euromonitor International." current="about">
  <div class="wrap page">
    <div class="top">
      <div>
        <h1>About</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          I lead Gen AI at Euromonitor International. My job is to make AI that market researchers and their clients can
          trust with real decisions.
        </p>
      </div>
      <Image class="portrait" src={portrait} alt="Black-and-white portrait of Lamine Lahouasnia" width={400} height={400} />
    </div>

    <div class="body prose">
      <h2>Now</h2>
      <p>
        I’m Director of Gen AI at Euromonitor International, based in Singapore. I lead the work that brings Gen AI into
        Passport, Euromonitor’s research platform. Passport AI launched in 2024 and answers client questions from
        Euromonitor’s own research rather than the open web, so every answer can be traced to its source. Since then
        we’ve added plain-English questions over Passport’s statistics and brought Passport into Microsoft 365 Copilot.
      </p>
      <p>
        From 2024 to 2026 I also ran Euromonitor’s Singapore office, the company’s hub for Southeast Asia: around
        seventy people from more than twenty countries.
      </p>

      <h2>How I got here</h2>
      <p>
        I grew up in London, studied economics at SOAS, and in 2005 moved to Beijing. I spent four years there as an
        analyst, an economics lecturer and a consultant helping companies enter the Chinese market, and picked up
        Mandarin along the way.
      </p>
      <p>
        I joined Euromonitor in 2009 and have been there ever since. I started in retail research, then led packaged
        food research, advising the world’s largest food companies and speaking at industry events. From 2017 I ran
        research technology alongside food and nutrition, which is where research, data and technology first came
        together for me. In 2021 I moved to Singapore to lead transformation, and in 2024 I took on Gen AI.
      </p>

      <h2>What I believe</h2>
      <p>
        Technology doesn’t replace expertise; it amplifies it. Most of what I <a href={url('/writing/')}>write</a> is
        about the gap between an AI answer that looks right and one that is right, and how to close it with trusted
        data, consistent methods and honest testing. I try to be as open about AI’s limits as about its successes,
        because that’s how trust is built.
      </p>

      <h2 id="building">What I’m building</h2>
      <p>
        Outside work I’m running a small, AI-native games studio. Its first game, <strong>The Moth House</strong>, is
        an eerie point-and-click puzzle game in the spirit of Rusty Lake. It’s deliberately a trial run: AI agents
        triage feedback, build and test from a work board, and I review and sign off each week. A second game, an
        office satire, is in design.
      </p>
      <p>
        The studio is how I learn, first-hand, where AI genuinely helps and where taste still has to come from a person.
        It’s the same question I work on every day, with lower stakes and more moths.
      </p>

      <h2>Away from the desk</h2>
      <p>
        I’m a Londoner with Algerian roots, living in Singapore with my family. I race the occasional sprint
        triathlon, play correspondence chess, volunteer with Food from the Heart, and have a soft spot for surrealist
        art.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="career" aria-labelledby="career-title">
      <h2 id="career-title">Career</h2>
      <ol>
        {career.map((c) => (
          <li>
            <span class="when">{c.when}</span>
            <span class="what">{c.what}</span>
            <span class="where">{c.where}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <p class="more">The full record is on <a href={SITE.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page { padding-top: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 4rem); }
  .top {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 13rem;
    gap: 2rem 3rem;
    align-items: end;
    max-width: 52rem;
  }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 7vw, 4.5rem); font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.04em; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .lede { font-size: 1.35rem; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0; max-width: 32rem; }
  .portrait { width: 13rem; border-radius: 2px; }
  .body { margin-top: 3rem; }
  .body h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }

  .career { margin-top: 4rem; max-width: 46rem; }
  .career h2 { font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.1rem); margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .career ol { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; position: relative; }
  .career ol::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0.3rem;
    top: 0.6rem;
    bottom: 0.6rem;
    width: 2px;
    background: var(--rule);
  }
  .career li {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 8rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.1rem 1.25rem;
    padding: 0 0 1.4rem 1.75rem;
    font-family: var(--sans);
  }
  .career li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.45rem;
    width: 0.75rem;
    height: 0.75rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 2px solid var(--ink-faint);
  }
  .career li:first-child::before { background: var(--blue); border-color: var(--blue); }
  .when { grid-row: span 2; color: var(--ink-faint); font-size: 0.95rem; padding-top: 0.1rem; }
  .what { font-weight: 650; line-height: 1.3; }
  .where { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .more { font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--ink-soft); margin-top: 0.5rem; }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .top { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .portrait { order: -1; width: 9rem; }
    .career li { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .when { grid-row: auto; }
  }
</style>
